[0.043, "o", "id: eec5193b-868a-4b62-b103-10a833680bf4\r\ntitle: Office Application Spawns Encoded PowerShell Download Cradle\r\nsource_url: tests/fixtures/article.html\r\nsummary: A macro-enabled Word document launches powershell.exe as a child of WINWORD.EXE\r\n  with an encoded command and hidden window options. The decoded command downloads\r\n  a second-stage script with Invoke-WebRequest and runs it with Invoke-Expression.\r\nattack_steps:\r\n- User opens Invoice_Q3_2026.docm from a phishing email and enables macros\r\n- AutoOpen routine uses WScript.Shell to start PowerShell\r\n- WINWORD.EXE spawns powershell.exe with -NoProfile -WindowStyle Hidden -ExecutionPolicy\r\n  Bypass -EncodedCommand <base64>\r\n- Decoded command calls Invoke-WebRequest against hxxp://update-cdn[.]example[.]net/st2.ps1\r\n  and pipes the response to Invoke-Expression\r\n- Second host variant uses the short form -enc\r\nindicators:\r\n- Invoice_Q3_2026.docm\r\n- WINWORD.EXE\r\n- powershell.exe\r\n- -EncodedCommand\r\n- -enc\r\n- -NoProfile\r\n- -WindowStyle Hidden\r\n"]
[0.000, "x", "0"]
